{"name":"Brioche","hex":"#dfcfc3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brioche","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of light sweet pastry or bun of French origin.","A knitted cushion for the feet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brioche"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brioche","blocks":[{"text":"Brioche is a Viennoiserie of French origin whose high egg and butter content gives it a rich and tender crumb. Chef Joël Robuchon described it as \"light and slightly puffy, more or less fine, according to the proportion of butter and eggs\". It has a dark, golden, flaky crust, frequently accentuated by an egg wash applied after proofing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Brioche.jpg/330px-Brioche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brioche","wikidata":"Q917574"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sicilian_brioche.jpg/500px-Sicilian_brioche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sicilian_brioche.jpg/1280px-Sicilian_brioche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sicilian_brioche.jpg/500px-Sicilian_brioche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sicilian Brioscia in the shape of a Brioche à tête","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASicilian_brioche.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Brioche_des_Rois_dsc06781.jpg/500px-Brioche_des_Rois_dsc06781.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Brioche_des_Rois_dsc06781.jpg/1280px-Brioche_des_Rois_dsc06781.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont